      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industries are broadly categorized based on Raw Material, Size, and Ownership structure.",
        "The Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956 served as the foundational economic policy emphasizing the public sector.",
        "The New Industrial Policy of 1991 marked a shift toward Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization (LPG).",
        "Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) are vital drivers of employment generation and balanced regional growth.",
        "Industrial Corridors and strategic government initiatives aim to overcome structural problems in Indian industrial development."
      ],
